# One line-ending policy for every checkout.
#
# Windows CI used to check out with core.autocrlf, turning scripts into CRLF and
# breaking a test that expected LF. With `text=auto eol=lf` a checkout matches
# the index on every OS: text is normalized to LF in the repository and checked
# out as LF, and Git's own binary detection keeps binary files untouched.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary artifacts that a future contribution may add. Normalizing these would
# corrupt them; none of them are tracked today, so this changes no existing file.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
